          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Network feed\n\nOne radio, three ways out.\n\n**Export** writes decoded events to a file on demand: CSV or JSON, for a spreadsheet or a script.\n\n**Event output** pushes every event as it happens to a webhook, MQTT broker or database. Its URL is empty on purpose. Fill it in and it starts sending; leave it and nothing leaves the machine.\n\n**Network IQ** is a different thing again: it sends the raw samples, not decodes, so another program on the network can demodulate them itself. The default address feeds a local listener on port 7355.\n\n**Map** keeps the aircraft on screen locally while all of that happens.\n\nTuned to 1090 MHz. Range here is about antenna height, not gain."
          },
          "position": { "x": 0.0, "y": 760.0 }
